<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edmund Pnischeck</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edmund Pnischeck was mayor of Lorch on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and head of the improvised administration of the Free State Bottleneck, the strip of land left unoccupied between the Allied bridgeheads at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koblenz">Koblenz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> from 1919 to 1923. Cut off from the rest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, his administration dealt with supply problems and smuggling until French troops occupied the area.</p></div>
